# Instructions for AI agents

## AI composition studio

When a task concerns compositions under `music/ai-compositions/`, the
published copies under `docs/compositions/`, the viewer under `docs/studio/`,
or the tools under `studio-tools/`, read and follow
`studio-tools/AGENT_INSTRUCTIONS.md` before doing anything else.

In short:

- Work only in those four directories. Do not modify, rename, move or delete
  anything else in this repository.
- Create and revise compositions only with `studio-tools/bin/studio`
  (`new` or `stage`, `prompt`, `run`, `render`, `accept`). Never edit a
  `version-NNNN/` directory, an accepted prompt or a manifest by hand.
- Save the user's prompt verbatim before doing the work.
- A composition is one complete Csound `.csd`. Follow the p-field
  conventions in `studio-tools/docs/csound-conventions.md`.
- Commit with `git add -- music/ai-compositions docs/compositions docs/studio studio-tools`,
  never `git add -A`.
- Do not merge, deploy or change repository settings unless asked. Publish
  (`studio publish`) only when asked.
- Report what you ran and what it printed. Do not claim that something
  works unless you ran it.

## Cursor Cloud specific instructions

- The environment is prepared by `studio-tools/cloud/install.sh`. The
  `studio` command loads `~/.local/ai-composition-studio/studio-env.sh` by
  itself; no shell setup is needed.
- At the start of a run, execute `studio-tools/bin/studio env`. If Csound 7
  is not found, run `bash studio-tools/cloud/install.sh` and then
  `studio-tools/cloud/check.sh`, and report the result before composing.
- Nothing outside the repository survives the run. Commit and push every
  accepted version, with its audio, before finishing.
- If another branch has revised the same composition, integrate with
  `studio adopt` as described in `studio-tools/docs/cloud-agents.md`. Do
  not resolve conflicts in `music/ai-compositions/` by hand.
